ssly associated migrants with violence. In office, however, her approach sh=
ifted.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333=
;margin:0 0 15px"><span>When she came to power in 2022, the E.U=E2=80=99s i=
mmigration policy centered on finding means to =E2=80=9Cspread the burden=
=E2=80=9D =E2=80=94 essentially distributing migrants across member states =
rather than reducing their flow. That has changed, due in part to Meloni, w=
ho led the E.U. in a hard line against asylum seekers and illegal migrants,=
 attempting to offshore their processing, a procedure that now has European=
 support.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#=
333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>She has also, however, pushed the continent to s=
ee Africa as a land of potential rather than problems. Under a plan adopted=
